+// THE AMBIENCE'S DISTANCE (patch 0037, the user, 2026-10-08: "a distance setting on how far out
+// the stuff renders and it needs to ... have a gradual fade out rather than a harsh cutoff ...
+// This would control the end of the fade-off distance. It still needs to be gradual regardless, and
+// it probably needs to span quite a ways"). The row sets where the fade ENDS; it begins at a fifth
+// of that, so the dust thins over most of its reach and is gone at the end. The fade is measured
+// from the eye, never from the surface behind a mote (0035 measured it to the surface, so the
+// motes in front of a near wall faded out). A long reach takes longer steps, at most 128 of them
+// to a ray; the far motes it then misses are the ones the fade has all but taken already.
+static const float AmbienceFadeStart = 0.2f;  // the share of the distance where the fade begins
+static const uint DustMaxSteps = 128;
+static const uint DustMaxMovers = 4;          // the movers near one ray that push the motes it passes
+
 float3 dustInLight(float3 origin, float3 direction, float end, uint2 launchIndex, float density, float visibility, bool outdoors) {
-    const float range = min(end, DustRange);
